from pathlib import Path
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
p=root/'README.md';s=p.read_text()
old='- **FX / EDIT:** Effects and channel EQ. REVERB offers SPRING (short, bright), HALL (longer tail) and ROOM (controlled short ambience) tonal presets of the shared reverb engine. Turn K1 to select a type, K2 DECAY, K3 SIZE and K4 MIX. MIX 0 is the unchanged dry sound; MIX 100 is the reverb return only (not a volume control). The return has been gain-balanced to stay audible even fully wet. The reverb still uses the same shared memory/taps and does not add an extra processor per voice.'
new='- **FX / EDIT:** Effects and channel EQ. REVERB now contains **three genuinely independent processing algorithms**, not SIZE/DECAY presets: **SPRING** uses a dispersive all-pass lattice and alternating-polarity feedback for metallic twang, **HALL** uses a Schroeder-style diffuser feeding a damped late-reflection tank, and **ROOM** uses separately spaced early wall reflections with a short comb tail. K1 selects the engine WITHOUT resetting your current parameters; K2 controls DECAY, K3 SIZE and K4 MIX. MIX 0 is unchanged dry signal, MIX 100 is 100% processed wet return. The three engines share the existing fixed 4096-sample memory and 64-sample diffuser, but only one algorithm executes at a time, globally after voice mixing. No extra synth voice or audio buffer is allocated. Each patch and project now remembers the reverb engine choice via unused bits of the existing routing setting. Old projects still load (legacy route 0/1 maps to HALL), but older firmware releases may reject projects saved with SPRING or ROOM selected, so back up before downgrading.'
assert s.count(old)==1;s=s.replace(old,new).replace('`RUPTURE-V1.77.fwsc`','`RUPTURE-V1.78.fwsc`');p.write_text(s)
p=root/'CHEAT-SHEET.html';s=p.read_text()
old='<section><h2>REVERB TYPES AND TRUE WET MIX</h2><p>FX → REVERB: K1 selects SPRING, HALL or ROOM tonal presets, K2 sets DECAY, K3 SIZE and K4 MIX. Each type has different length, early reflections and density from the existing global tank. MIX 0 is dry only, MIX 100 is wet only; more MIX is not simply a master-volume reduction. No extra effect buffer or per-voice processor is used.</p></section>'
new='<section><h2>THREE REVERB ENGINES (V1.78)</h2><p>FX → REVERB: K1 selects one of three independent algorithms, NOT different parameter presets: SPRING is a dispersive metallic feedback/allpass design; HALL uses an allpass diffuser and long low-pass late tail; ROOM uses discrete early reflections plus a short comb tail. K2 DECAY, K3 SIZE, K4 MIX are independent and stay at your settings on a type change. MIX 0 is dry only, MIX 100 wet only. Only one global engine runs, using the same fixed SRAM tank and no new synth voices or buffers. Engine choice is stored in projects/presets. Older projects default to HALL; older firmware may not accept newly saved SPRING/ROOM projects.</p></section>'
assert s.count(old)==1;s=s.replace(old,new);p.write_text(s)
p=root/'CHANGELOG.md';s=p.read_text();s='''# RUPTURE V1.78 — Three Independent Reverb Engines

- Replaced the previous single shared reverb algorithm with three **different real DSP topologies**: SPRING (dispersive allpass + inharmonic sign-alternating feedback), HALL (Schroeder diffusion + filtered multi-tap late-feedback tank), ROOM (sparse specular early reflections + short damped feedback comb).
- K1 selects the algorithm without overwriting the user's SIZE or DECAY; K2 = DECAY, K3 = SIZE, K4 = true 0–100% dry/wet. At full wet there is no direct oscillator feed. Only one algorithm runs per sample.
- The three engines use the existing 4096-sample reverb ring, 64-sample diffuser and filter states; no new SRAM, effect instances, per-voice work or external dependencies. Actual FM1 DSP/DMA performance remains subject to physical measurement.
- The selected engine is now saved for project-global and per-preset FX by using two previously-unused bits of the existing 1-byte routing field, retaining the PJT34 record length and CRC. Legacy routing values 0/1 decode as HALL and remain loadable. Older RUPTURE releases may reject **newly saved** projects with SPRING or ROOM, so make backups before downgrading.
- The 16-KiB protected bootheader, trusted OTA loader, OTA native code, device identity and all other synthesizer and sequencer modules are preserved.
- See `docs/TEST-V1.78.md` for host DSP, storage, throughput and firmware verification. Not physically verified on FM1.

'''+s;p.write_text(s)
p=root/'WEBSITE-DEPLOY.md';s=p.read_text().replace('V1.77','V1.78');p.write_text(s)
print('V1.78 README, cheat-sheet, changelog, website deploy docs updated')
